erDiagram

%% The same order book, revealed a step at a time.
%% All three of this kind's timeline targets are named below: an entity —
%% under the name its author wrote, never the alias its box draws — a
%% relationship, under the `${from}:${to}` id the model assigns it, and a
%% `subgraph` cluster, under the `subgraph:N` id the model mints for it. The
%% colon is this kind's own separator: the other four join a connector's
%% endpoints with `-`, which an ER entity name is allowed to contain and
%% theirs are not.
%% A cluster's name is not its id (ADR-0010): the frame below is titled
%% `fulfilment`, which is what it draws, and addressed as `subgraph:1`,
%% which is what a timeline entry has to say.
%% An attribute is not a target: its cells are drawn inside the entity's own
%% group, so the box that owns a row is what animates it.

CUSTOMER["Customer Account"] {
  string id PK
  string name
}

CUSTOMER ||--o{ ORDER : places

subgraph fulfilment
  ORDER ||--|{ LINE-ITEM : contains
end

timeline:
  enter CUSTOMER fade
  enter ORDER slide-top, enter CUSTOMER:ORDER fade
  enter subgraph:1 fade, enter LINE-ITEM slide-right, enter ORDER:LINE-ITEM fade
  highlight CUSTOMER outline
  highlight CUSTOMER:ORDER glow, unhighlight CUSTOMER
  exit ORDER:LINE-ITEM fade, exit LINE-ITEM slide-right
